    schema:description "CreatorIQ is the operating system for creator-led growth trusted by more than 1,300 global brands and agencies. We’re on a mission to make businesses more human, and humans more impactful. We operate by our values — be intentional, pursue excellence every day, embrace the journey together, and be a good human — every day. CreatorIQ has earned the title of best companies to work for in multiple programs, including BuiltIn LA and NY. It’s been named a Fastest-Growing Company in North America on the Deloitte Technology Fast 500™ for four years, was named a leader in IDC MarketScape: Worldwide Influencer Marketing Platforms for Large Enterprises in 2025, was named a Leader by The Forrester New Wave™: Influencer Marketing Solutions, and has been consistently recognized by G2 as a Leader, and is rated 5 stars on Influencer MarketingHub. We operate in a flexible work model that combines both in-person and remote work to boost collaboration, enhance innovation, and adapt to individual work styles. We're seeking passionate, innovative minds to join our journey. Be a part of our dynamic team and let's transform the industry together! Director, International Revenue Growth CreatorIQ is seeking a Director or Senior Director, International Revenue Growth to build and own the marketing, pipeline, and revenue growth function across Europe, the Middle East, and Asia-Pacific. Reporting to the VP of Revenue Marketing, this leader will be responsible for generating demand across priority international markets while serving as a strategic revenue partner to regional sales. They will work closely with enterprise sales leaders and sellers to shape go-to-market strategy for a defined set of critical accounts, create account-specific growth plans, and accelerate high-value opportunities. The role will initially launch with support from a U.S.-based marketing team and a network of contractors. Over time, this leader will define the regional organization, hire people on the ground, and build a scalable international growth function. This role may be based in either the UK or the Netherlands. It requires travel to London at least monthly, as well as regular travel to customer meetings, team gatherings, and field events across Europe and Asia-Pacific. The successful candidate will combine strategic thinking, hands-on execution, strong enterprise sales partnership, and deep knowledge of the commercial and cultural nuances of European and Asia-Pacific markets. They will help CreatorIQ support its initial $8M international revenue goal while building the pipeline, operating model, and team required for the next stage of growth. The final title, Director or Senior Director, will be determined based on the selected candidate’s experience, leadership background, scope, and demonstrated ability to build and scale an international revenue growth function. This is a remote role based in the UK, with travel to London approximately 1–2 times per month. The role also requires regular travel across Europe for events and occasional travel to the Asia-Pacific region. In this role, you’ll get to: Build and own CreatorIQ’s international revenue growth engine across Europe, the Middle East, and Asia-Pacific, establishing the regional strategy, priorities, operating rhythm, resource plan, and measurement framework across key markets. Generate net-new demand through integrated regional growth programs spanning account-based marketing, field marketing, executive engagement, events, partner activation, seller enablement, localized campaigns, and priority-account plays. Serve as the strategic revenue partner to the RVP of International Sales, regional sales leaders, and enterprise sellers, aligning on market priorities, account coverage, pipeline goals, opportunity strategy, and actions required to accelerate growth. Own the growth strategy for a defined set of critical enterprise accounts, partnering with sellers to identify buying-group priorities, shape account plans, coordinate targeted marketing support, and create account-specific engagement programs. Help accelerate high-value opportunities by activating executive and customer engagement, developing relevant regional messaging and proof points, supporting buying committees, and removing marketing-related barriers throughout the sales cycle. Define CreatorIQ’s strongest product-market fit and right to win by country, industry, vertical, customer segment, and account type, using customer insight, seller feedback, market data, competitive intelligence, and performance signals to focus investment. Bring a nuanced understanding of European and Asia-Pacific markets into go-to-market decisions, adapting strategy, messaging, events, channels, and seller support to reflect differences in buying behavior, market maturity, business culture, procurement processes, and local conditions. Establish a clear operating cadence with sales around target-account selection, pipeline creation, opportunity progression, campaign performance, forecast risk, and next-best actions for priority accounts. Launch the function with support from U.S.-based marketing partners and specialized contractors, creating clear ownership, processes, standards, and accountability across a distributed team. Build the long-term regional organization by defining the talent plan, hiring people in priority markets, and developing a high-performing on-the-ground international revenue growth team. Deliver measurable revenue impact by supporting the initial $8M international revenue goal and building future pipeline; define KPIs, review performance, share insights, and reallocate resources toward the highest-return opportunities. Who you are and what you’ll need for this position: 8+ years of experience in B2B SaaS growth, demand generation, revenue marketing, account-based marketing, field marketing, or go-to-market leadership, with a demonstrated record of creating pipeline and revenue impact across international markets. Significant experience partnering directly with enterprise sales leaders and sellers in complex B2B sales environments, with a strong understanding of long sales cycles, multiple stakeholders, account planning, pipeline inspection, forecasting, and opportunity progression. A demonstrated ability to both generate net-new demand and influence the acceleration of complex enterprise opportunities, with clear accountability for pipeline creation, pipeline quality, and revenue outcomes. Experience working on a named-account or strategic-account basis, including account selection, buying-committee strategy, executive engagement, opportunity reviews, account-specific campaigns, and coordinated pursuit plans. Deep familiarity with the commercial and cultural nuances of European and Asia-Pacific markets, with the ability to adapt go-to-market strategy by country and region rather than apply a single global playbook. Experience building or scaling a regional growth function, including evaluating product-market fit, prioritizing countries and customer segments, and translating market strategy into executable programs. Hands-on expertise across integrated growth channels, including ABM, field and event marketing, partner programs, seller enablement, executive programs, localized campaigns, and digital demand generation. Experience building a new function from the ground up, including leading through contractors and shared resources initially, then hiring, developing, and scaling a regional team. Strong commercial judgment and the credibility to advise, challenge, and support sales leadership as a true revenue partner rather than simply respond to campaign requests. An analytical, highly collaborative, and culturally aware leadership style, with excellent communication, prioritization, and stakeholder-management skills. Comfort operating across time zones, ambiguity, distributed teams, frequent travel, and a fast-moving global environment. Based in the UK or the Netherlands, with the ability to travel to London at least monthly and regularly attend customer meetings, partner engagements, team gatherings, and field events across Europe and Asia-Pacific. Confidence can sometimes hold us back from applying for a job. But we'll let you in on a secret: there's no such thing as a 'perfect' candidate. Have 50% of the criteria? Excited about this opportunity? Passionate about what we do at CreatorIQ? Please apply! CreatorIQ is a place where everyone can grow. What you will get from us: People: work with talented, collaborative, and friendly people who love what they do. Guidance: utilize our learning platform to fully get the training and tools you’ll need to become successful here from your first day with us. Surprise meal stipends: work from home can’t stop the enjoyment of someone else making a meal for you! Work/life harmony: 15 days vacation, floating and set holidays, wellness allowance, and paid parental leave. Whole Health Package: medical, dental, vision, life, disability insurance, and more. Savings: a 401k (USA) plan to help you plan ahead. Work from home stipend: to assist you in setting up a home office that works for you (or buy a new dog leash - your choice!). Who we are: CreatorIQ is the operating system for creator-led growth, helping global brands and agencies transform creator marketing into an intelligence-driven growth engine. Powered by the Creator Graph™, which processes more than 250 million social posts daily across more than 15 million creators worldwide, CreatorIQ unifies fragmented platform data into a centralized intelligence layer and system of record for creator relationships, performance, governance, and commerce. More than 1,300 organizations—including Dentsu, Delta Air Lines, Google, Beiersdorf, Nestlé, and Wella—rely on CreatorIQ as the infrastructure to run and scale their creator programs globally. CreatorIQ is a global company headquartered in Los Angeles with offices in Austin, New York, San Francisco, London, Manila, and Warsaw. Learn more at www.creatoriq.com and follow us on LinkedIn and Instagram. At CreatorIQ, we believe that diversity is the key to unlocking our full potential. We are committed to fostering an inclusive, equitable, and empowering work environment where everyone can thrive, regardless of race, ethnicity, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, disability, or any other characteristic that makes us unique. By embracing our core values of being intentional, pursuing excellence every day, embracing the journey together, being a good human, and staying focused on what’s important, we create an atmosphere that promotes collaboration and growth. Join us to celebrate differences, innovate together, and be a part of a business that is disrupting the marketing industry. Compensation, benefits, and beyond: We understand that a comprehensive benefits package plays a significant role in your overall compensation. To gain more insight into the various components of our total compensation, we invite you to review our benefits and perks. AI Transparency Notice We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications and note taking during interviews. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please refer to our Global Candidate Privacy Notice. Compensation: £98K – £128K • Offers Equity • £98K – £128K • Offers Equity Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
