    schema:description "Your role at Ocumeda We are looking for a Product Owner - Medical AI (m/f/d) to take ownership of a new AI-based medical device. You will own the product's technical specification, backlog and requirements end-to-end, from feature scoping through implementation and international roll-out, acting as the central point between our medical, regulatory, and AI team. If you're motivated to take ownership of a product and shape it within a growing MedTech company, this role is for you. Own the product end-to-end: from feature scoping through implementation, launch, and international roll-out Translate medical and business requirements into clear technical specifications and a prioritized backlog, based on input from users, markets, and internal stakeholders Support the MDR process by bringing technical and product input into Regulatory's decisions on intended use, risk, and output presentation Own the software requirements specification (SRS) and work closely with our AI team to specify and integrate the MDR-certified AI system into the product Work with the product team to bring the device live across multiple markets on our existing platform, adapting to local requirements where needed What makes you a great fit You have a technical background or hands-on experience with software/API specifications, and you're comfortable moving fluidly between technical AI/engineering details and the regulatory, medical, and business perspectives, translating in both directions You are motivated to work hands-on in a startup environment, balancing pragmatism with structure You take ownership, work in a structured way, and have the drive to push things forward, while collaborating closely with the team. You collaborate closely with the medical, regulatory and AI team to ensure smooth execution and alignment. You are fluent in English (additional languages are a plus, but not required) You bring relevant experience in product management or a comparable role, ideally with exposure to AI products, regulated environments (e.g. MDR), or internationalization What you can expect from us Flexible working hours and hybrid work with home office options Subsidized Deutschlandticket (public transport pass) for employees Personal learning & development budget for trainings, conferences, and professional growth High level of ownership, fast decision-making, and real opportunities to help shape the company Regular feedback, short decision paths, and individual development opportunities International team with close collaboration, regular exchange, and shared team events Collaboration with experts from optometry, ophthalmology, software & AI development, and strategy consulting Monthly contribution toward a Wellpass membership Free access to Nilo Health for mental health and wellbeing Competitive salary matching your role and experience Modern, dog-friendly office in the heart of Munich, close to the main train station (Hauptbahnhof) Contributing to a leading teleophthalmology platform that sustainably improves access to eye care Established B2B2C model with over 800 partner optician locations and more than 500,000 screenings performed Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
