    schema:description "About us At Trainline, our purpose is to empower greener travel choices, connecting people and places. Trainline enables millions of travellers to find and book the best value tickets across carriers, fares, and journey options through our highly rated mobile app, website, and B2B partner channels. Great journeys start with Trainline 🚄 We’re Europe’s leading independent rail platform, helping millions of travellers find and book the best-value rail and coach journeys across our app, website and partner channels. Our job is to make the green travel choice the best choice. By building a better train travel experience, we help more people choose rail - creating a positive impact for customers, our business and the planet. We’re a team of more than 1,000 Trainliners from over 50 nationalities, working across London, Paris, Barcelona, Milan, Edinburgh and Madrid. Now is a brilliant time to join us and help shape the future of travel. Introducing the Trainline Customer Growth Team 👋 We're looking for a Senior Engineering Manager to lead engineering within our Customer Growth pillar, on the Value and Growth side of the business. You'll oversee an organisation comprising Engineering Managers and multiple fullstack squads, spanning web, backend and mobile, our current focus is across railcards growth, railcards retention and adoption, subscriptions, and customer value exchange, which shapes how we structure and present our offering to customers. You'll partner closely with Product, Design, Data and Commercial to align technical delivery with business outcomes and play a key role in how Trainline communicates value and pricing to customers. We're looking for a leader who can bring together several distinct but connected domains, empower their teams, and balance commercial impact with customer-first thinking. In this role as the Senior Engineering Manager, you will... 🚄 Lead multiple squads and their Engineering Managers, supporting career development through coaching and performance conversations Own end-to-end delivery across your squads, helping ensure projects are planned, executed and delivered to a high standard and on time Partner closely with Product, Design, Data and Commercial to align technical delivery with business outcomes, using domain expertise to guide teams toward high-impact opportunities Guide technical direction and architecture across fullstack web, backend and mobile squads, without needing to be deeply hands-on with code Bring coherence across distinct areas, railcards growth and retention, subscriptions and customer value exchange, ensuring technical strategy connects them where it matters Champion engineering best practices across teams, promoting quality and a culture of technical innovation Drive operational excellence, ensuring teams have robust monitoring, alerting and incident management processes in place We'd love to hear from you if you have... 🔍 Experience leading engineering teams and delivering complex, multi-team initiatives A strong track record of developing people, building high-performing teams and growing future leaders The ability to inspire trust and autonomy at all levels, fostering a positive, inclusive and high-performing team culture Comfort operating across multiple, distinct product domains and connecting them into a coherent technical strategy Enjoyment working in a dynamic, collaborative and highly cross-functional environment Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence at all levels of the organisation Confidence leading through ambiguity, creating clarity and momentum in complex or uncertain situations More information: Enjoy fantastic perks like private healthcare & dental insurance, a generous work from abroad policy, 2-for-1 share purchase plans, an EV Scheme to further reduce carbon emissions, extra festive time off, and excellent family-friendly benefits. We prioritise career growth with clear career paths, transparent pay bands, personal learning budgets, and regular learning days. Jump on board and supercharge your career from day one! We're operating a hybrid model and ask that Trainliners work from the office a minimum of 60% of their time over a 12-week period. We also have a 28-day Work from Abroad policy. Our values represent the things that matter most to us and what we live and breathe everyday, in everything we do: 💭 Think Big - We're building the future of rail ✔️ Own It - We focus on every customer, partner and journey 🤝 Travel Together - We're one team ♻️ Do Good - We make a positive impact We know that having a diverse team makes us better and helps us succeed. And we mean all forms of diversity - gender, ethnicity, sexuality, disability, nationality and diversity of thought. That's why we're committed to creating inclusive places to work, where everyone belongs and differences are valued and celebrated. Interested in finding out more about what it's like to work at Trainline? Why not check us out on LinkedIn, Instagram and Glassdoor! Compensation: £120K – £135K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus • Base salary £120K – £135K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
