    schema:description "<p><strong>Location:</strong> hybrid, based at one of our UK offices: London, Cardiff, or Manchester.&nbsp;</p> <h2>The Role</h2> <p>As a key member of the Global People Operations team, the UK People Operations Coordinator provides end-to-end operational HR support across a diverse UK portfolio. The role has primary employee-lifecycle ownership for Strategy &amp; Communications, People Advisory and Corporate Functions, and coordinates onboarding and offboarding activities for Financial Advisory and Management Consulting. As a first point of contact for employees and managers, the role holder manages a broad range of enquiries, transactions and cases, applying sound judgement, resilience and a strong service mindset. The successful candidate will be a proactive self-starter with HR generalist experience who can build effective stakeholder relationships, manage competing priorities and identify opportunities to simplify and improve how services are delivered.&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>Responsibilities&nbsp;</strong></p> <ul> <li>Own and manage the employee lifecycle for Strategy &amp; Communications, People Advisory and Corporate Functions, including onboarding, probation, family leave, absence and wellbeing cases, Visa and immigration, job and contractual changes, internal transfers and offboarding.&nbsp;</li> <li>Coordinate onboarding and offboarding for Financial Advisory and Management Consulting, ensuring candidates, employees, managers and relevant internal teams understand responsibilities, deadlines and next steps.&nbsp;</li> <li>Manage business-specific onboarding and offboarding requirements, including different contractual and compensation terms, templates, approvals and downstream actions, while identifying opportunities to align and simplify processes.&nbsp;</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Act as a first point of contact for employees and managers, independently resolving a broad range of routine and moderately complex people-related queries. Promote and educate stakeholders on available self-service tools, resources and processes, while providing additional guidance and support where required. Exercise sound judgement in identifying and appropriately escalating sensitive, high-risk or specialist matters to the relevant People Team colleagues.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Manage employment changes such as promotions, salary and allowance changes, flexible working arrangements, changes to hours or location, and internal and international transfers, ensuring documentation, approvals and Workday records are complete and accurate.&nbsp;</li> <li>Prepare contractor agreements and coordinate contractor onboarding and offboarding in Workday. Conduct appropriate checks to support the correct engagement and classification of contingent workers, guide managers through the completion of CEST assessments where required.</li> <li>Provide support, both to employees and the wider People Team, during cyclical process such as Goal Setting, and Performance, Promotion and Compensation reviews. Such support varies by process but may involve leading training sessions for employees, providing Workday assistance, or tracking completion rates.</li> <li>Monitor case queues, lifecycle trackers and deadlines, proactively managing workload, identifying risks and providing clear updates to stakeholders.&nbsp;</li> <li>Collaborate with Payroll, Reward, HRIS, Recruitment, IT and other internal teams to ensure accurate and timely delivery of employee-lifecycle processes. Route benefits queries to the Reward team and provide operational support where agreed.&nbsp;</li> <li>Serve as a front-end subject matter expert for Workday and a confident back-end user, providing practical guidance, resolving issues, completing transactions and maintaining high standards of data quality.&nbsp;</li> <li>Anticipate reporting needs and work with HRIS and other stakeholders to improve reporting, data quality and management information.&nbsp;</li> <li>Build effective cover arrangements and share knowledge across the UK People Operations team to strengthen resilience during peak periods and absences.&nbsp;</li> <li>Handle personal and confidential information with integrity, discretion and appropriate data-protection controls.&nbsp;</li> <li>Proactively contribute to the continuous improvement of HR policies, processes and related documentation/guides to enhance People Operations services and the employee experience.</li> </ul> <h2>Requirements</h2> <ul> <li>At least 2 years’ experience as an HR Generalist</li> <li>Knowledge of local employment legislation.</li> <li>Experience with HRIS systems like Workday preferred.</li> <li>Bachelor's degree in human resources, business management, psychology or CIPD Level 3 or 5 qualification is highly regarded</li> <li>Strong administration and organizational skills with excellent attention to detail</li> <li>Exceptional customer service and prioritization skills</li> <li>Ability to manage multiple tasks and projects simultaneously</li> <li>Excellent verbal and written communication skills</li> <li>Exemplifies integrity and discretion</li> <li>Continuous improvement mindset – a proactive, adaptable, and agile collaborator.</li> <li>Proficient in Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint)</li> </ul> <h2>What We Can Offer</h2> <ul> <li>Competitive salary (depending on experience)</li> <li>28 days holiday</li> <li>Discretionary bonus</li> <li>Annual salary review</li> <li>Pension (with company contribution: 5% of annual salary)</li> <li>Enhanced maternity and paternity leave (depending on length of service) and shared parental leave</li> <li>Private medical insurance</li> <li>Group Income protection</li> <li>Life assurance</li> <li>Cycle to work schemes</li> <li>Season ticket loans</li> <li>Regular social, cultural and charitable activities</li> <li>Flexible working with office laptop and phone provided</li> </ul> <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p> <p><strong>About Teneo</strong></p> <p>Teneo is the global CEO advisory firm. We partner with our clients globally to do great things for a better future.</p> <p>Drawing upon our global team and expansive network of senior advisors, we provide advisory services across our five business segments on a stand-alone or fully integrated basis to help our clients solve complex business challenges. Our clients include a significant number of the Fortune 100 and FTSE 100, as well as other corporations, financial institutions and organizations.</p> <p>Our full range of advisory services includes strategic communications, investor relations, financial transactions and restructuring, management consulting, physical and cyber risk, organizational design, board and executive search, geopolitics and government affairs, corporate governance and ESG.</p> <p>The firm has more than 2,000 employees located in 50+ offices around the world.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>#LI-Hybrid</p> Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
