    schema:description "What We Do Rillet serves accounting and finance teams, the financial brains of their companies. Our job is to help them run the numbers with impossible speed, accuracy, and insight. Rillet is the AI-native ERP built for modern finance teams. We help companies automate the most critical parts of finance, from closing the books and recognizing revenue to consolidating entities and reporting to investors. More than 600 companies run on Rillet, including Mercor, Scribe, and Function Health, and we partner with leading accounting firms including EY and KPMG. This huge market is ours to take. We’ve raised $200M+ from Sequoia, a16z, ICONIQ, Bain Capital Ventures, Oak HC/FT, and other leading investors to build the financial infrastructure for the next generation of companies and help every business run its numbers at the speed of AI. Who We Are Rillet’s pace is not for everyone. Intelligence is table stakes. To succeed here, you need extreme speed, agency, and flexibility. The people who thrive at Rillet do not wait for assignments. They internalize the mission, design a strategy, and bring back results that are better, faster, and more creative than a manager could have asked for. Our work revolves around our customers. The people who succeed here are energized by delivering what matters most, even when it was not part of the original plan. Rillet is built on deep accounting expertise, and it takes people from many disciplines to build a category-defining company. You do not need to be an accountant to thrive here. You do need to care deeply about the problems we solve and the impact our customers can create. Together, we combine the precision of accounting with the speed, creativity, and ambition of AI-native software to power the financial core of the world’s fastest-growing companies while redefining what finance teams should expect from their software. Who We Need We are building industry-defining accounting and finance software, and we’re looking for a Solutions Consultant to help Rillet enter its next phase of growth. We’ve grown quickly and are expanding our GTM team to accelerate that trajectory. You’ll work closely with Sales, Product, and company leadership to help prospective customers evaluate Rillet as their next ERP. As an early member of Rillet’s UK GTM team, you’ll be uniquely positioned to shape how we sell, test new approaches, and help build the foundation for Rillet’s go-to-market motion in the UK. What You'll Do Remove technical and accounting objections. Play a key role throughout the sales cycle by helping prospective customers evaluate Rillet from both a technical and accounting perspective. You’ll understand their business requirements, accounting processes, and existing technology stack; explain how Rillet fits into their environment; and show how it can improve the way their finance team operates. Deliver tailored product demonstrations. Configure sandbox environments and tailor demonstrations around each prospect’s specific workflows and use cases. You’ll run high-impact demos, answer detailed questions in real time, and adapt your approach based on the customer’s priorities. You’ll act as a trusted consultant throughout the evaluation process. Become a product and domain expert. Develop a deep understanding of Rillet, accounting workflows, and the broader technology ecosystem used by modern finance teams. You’ll be able to answer the vast majority of product, accounting, and technical questions directly without needing to rely on the Product team. Execute with urgency. Work cross-functionally to provide front-line prospect feedback to Sales, Product, Engineering, and company leadership in near real time. Experiment with different demo approaches, contribute to thoughtful customer follow-ups, and help accelerate opportunities through the sales process. Represent Rillet. Be a trusted face of the company, bringing high customer empathy and structured problem-solving to every prospect interaction. You’ll engage with sophisticated finance and accounting leaders and continue to deepen your expertise in the domain. Who We're Looking For Strong professional experience in accounting, with exposure to areas such as revenue recognition, financial close, reconciliations, and multi-entity consolidation. Experience supporting customer evaluations, implementations, solutions consulting, or customer-facing work involving accounting or financial software. Strong understanding of the systems and technology used by modern finance and accounting teams. Familiarity with IFRS and/or UK GAAP and the ability to speak credibly with senior finance and accounting stakeholders. Excellent communicator who can make complex accounting and technical concepts easy to understand and communicate in a clear, conversational way. Comfortable moving between accounting, product, and technical conversations with different stakeholders. Thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced environment while maintaining high attention to detail. Proactive, highly responsive, and comfortable taking ownership in an early-stage environment. ACA, ACCA, CIMA, or equivalent accounting qualification, or experience beginning your career in audit or accounting advisory, is a plus. Life at Rillet Grow with us. Take meaningful ownership, expand your scope, and make an impact as Rillet scales. Competitive pay and meaningful equity. Be rewarded for the value you help create. Benefits that support you. We offer competitive benefits designed to support your health, wellbeing, time away from work, family, and long-term financial goals. Better together. We value collaboration, connection, and spending meaningful time together as a team. We regularly create opportunities to connect through team meals, events, and company gatherings. Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
